    "content": {
      "question_html": "<p>25.0 cm<sup>3</sup> of 1.00 mol dm<sup>−3</sup> hydrochloric acid is added to 25.0 cm<sup>3</sup> of 1.00 mol dm<sup>−3</sup> sodium hydroxide in a polystyrene cup. The temperature rises by 6.8 °C.</p>\n<div class=\"q-line\"><div class=\"q-line__text\">Calculate the enthalpy change of neutralisation, in kJ mol<sup>−1</sup>. Assume the solution has a density of 1.00 g cm<sup>−3</sup> and a specific heat capacity of 4.18 J g<sup>−1</sup> K<sup>−1</sup>.</div><span class=\"q-marks\">(5)</span></div>",
      "question_image_url": null,
      "mark_scheme_html": "<div class=\"q-line\"><div class=\"q-line__text\">q = mcΔT = 50.0 × 4.18 × 6.8</div><span class=\"ms-codes\">(1)</span></div>\n<div class=\"q-line\"><div class=\"q-line__text\">= 1421 J</div><span class=\"ms-codes\">(1)</span></div>\n<div class=\"q-line\"><div class=\"q-line__text\">Amount of water formed = 0.0250 mol</div><span class=\"ms-codes\">(1)</span></div>\n<div class=\"q-line\"><div class=\"q-line__text\">ΔH = <span class=\"frac\"><span class=\"frac__n\">1421</span><span class=\"frac__d\">0.0250</span></span> = 56 800 J mol<sup>−1</sup></div><span class=\"ms-codes\">(1)</span></div>\n<div class=\"q-line\"><div class=\"q-line__text\">ΔH = −56.8 kJ mol<sup>−1</sup> (sign required)</div><span class=\"ms-codes\">(1)</span></div>",
      "mark_scheme_image_url": null
    }
  },
