    "content": {
      "question_html": "<div class=\"q-part\"><span class=\"q-part__label\">(a)</span><div class=\"q-part__body\">Calculate the pH of 0.0150 mol dm<sup>−3</sup> hydrochloric acid.</div><span class=\"q-marks\">(1)</span></div>\n<div class=\"q-part\"><span class=\"q-part__label\">(b)</span><div class=\"q-part__body\">Calculate the pH of 0.100 mol dm<sup>−3</sup> ethanoic acid. K<sub>a</sub> = 1.74 × 10<sup>−5</sup> mol dm<sup>−3</sup>.</div><span class=\"q-marks\">(3)</span></div>\n<div class=\"q-part\"><span class=\"q-part__label\">(c)</span><div class=\"q-part__body\">Explain how a solution containing ethanoic acid and sodium ethanoate resists a change in pH when a small amount of acid is added.</div><span class=\"q-marks\">(2)</span></div>",
      "question_image_url": null,
      "mark_scheme_html": "<div class=\"q-part\"><span class=\"q-part__label\">(a)</span><div class=\"q-part__body\">pH = −log(0.0150) = 1.82</div><span class=\"ms-codes\">(1)</span></div>\n<div class=\"q-part\"><span class=\"q-part__label\">(b)</span><div class=\"q-part__body\">[H<sup>+</sup>] = √(K<sub>a</sub> × [HA])</div><span class=\"ms-codes\">(1)</span></div>\n<div class=\"q-line\"><div class=\"q-line__text\">[H<sup>+</sup>] = 1.32 × 10<sup>−3</sup> mol dm<sup>−3</sup></div><span class=\"ms-codes\">(1)</span></div>\n<div class=\"q-line\"><div class=\"q-line__text\">pH = 2.88</div><span class=\"ms-codes\">(1)</span></div>\n<div class=\"q-part\"><span class=\"q-part__label\">(c)</span><div class=\"q-part__body\">The added H<sup>+</sup> ions react with ethanoate ions, CH<sub>3</sub>COO<sup>−</sup></div><span class=\"ms-codes\">(1)</span></div>\n<div class=\"q-line\"><div class=\"q-line__text\">The equilibrium CH<sub>3</sub>COOH ⇌ H<sup>+</sup> + CH<sub>3</sub>COO<sup>−</sup> shifts to the left, removing most of the added H<sup>+</sup></div><span class=\"ms-codes\">(1)</span></div>",
      "mark_scheme_image_url": null
    }
  },
